## Part 3 — The Home Screen

### Background: a random world each time
- Every time the Home Screen opens, the background is a **freshly generated, random world**: pick a new random seed (e.g. `crypto.getRandomValues` or `Math.random`) instead of `CFG.seed`. The seed must flow through the existing seeded noise/rng code (`math/noise.ts`, `math/random.ts`, `world/fields.ts`) — add a function such as `setWorldSeed(seed)` that rebuilds the noise fields, and call it before chunks are generated. Do not reorder existing `rng()` calls.
- The **camera slowly scrolls over the world** on its own: no player control, no player model visible (hide the player or don't place it), a smooth constant drift in one direction at a pleasant height/angle (add `CFG.home.scrollSpeed`, `CFG.home.cameraZoom`, `CFG.home.direction`; a gentle slow yaw sway is welcome). Chunks must keep streaming in ahead of the camera through `World.plan()` / `World.step()` the same way they do for the player, without hitches (respect `CHUNK_BATCH_MS`).
- The world under the Home Screen must render with the existing renderer, lights, fog and materials — same look as the game.
- `Input` must **not** be listening while the Home Screen is up; taps go to the cards only.

### The three cards
- Three cards placed **horizontally in a row**, centred on screen, separated by a **small gap** (≈ 12–16 px, use `clamp()`).
- Order and content (left → right):
  1. **"Play with friends!"** — a **globe icon** (represents online) at the **top centre** of the card. This card is **unavailable**: online is not set up yet. Show it visibly disabled (lower opacity / desaturated, `cursor: not-allowed`, `aria-disabled="true"`), with a small secondary line "Unavailable right now". Tapping it does nothing (optionally a tiny shake or a short "Coming soon" toast — no navigation).
  2. **"Survival"** — a **play icon** (▶ triangle) at the top centre. This card is the **middle one and must be bigger** than the other two (e.g. ~1.2× width and height; side cards vertically centred against it).
  3. **"Creative mode"** — a **tool icon** (🛠️ hammer + wrench) at the top centre.
- Draw the three icons as **inline SVG** (stroke icons, white, ~28–40 px, scaled up slightly on the middle card) so they look identical on every platform — do not rely on emoji glyphs.
- Labels use `font-family: var(--font)`, white text, centred under the icon.
- **No rounded corners**: `border-radius: 0` on the cards (and on anything inside them that shows an edge).
- **Glass look copied from the Alva repo's dialogs** (`alva/css/base.css` tokens and `.glass` / `.glass--panel` in `alva/css/battle.css`). Port these exact values into `src/style.css` as CSS custom properties and classes:
  ```css
  --glass-fill: rgba(10, 11, 13, 0.64);
  --glass-fill-panel: rgba(10, 11, 13, 0.86);
  --glass-fill-blur: rgba(10, 11, 13, 0.7);
  --glass-edge: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
  --glass-sheen: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.07), rgba(255,255,255,0.02) 45%, rgba(255,255,255,0) 75%);
  --glass-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.06), 0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.22);

  .glass--panel {
    background: var(--glass-sheen), var(--glass-fill-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-edge);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow), 0 12px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
  }
  @supports ((-webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) or (backdrop-filter: blur(1px))) {
    .glass--panel {
      background: var(--glass-sheen), var(--glass-fill-blur);
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px) saturate(1.1);
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px) saturate(1.1);
    }
  }
  ```
  (Check Alva's `--shadow-lg` value and use it instead of the placeholder shadow above.) The world must be visible, blurred, through the cards.
- Hover/focus (enabled cards only): slight lift (`translateY(-4px)`) and a brighter edge (`rgba(255,255,255,0.28)`), with a visible keyboard focus ring. Cards are `<button>` elements, reachable with Tab / arrow keys, activated with Enter/Space.

### Entrance animation: falling from the top
- When the white fades out, the three cards **fall in from above the top of the screen** to their resting positions.
- They all fall **together**, with only a **tiny stagger** between them (≈ 60–80 ms; left, then middle, then right). Add `CFG.home.cardFallMs` (≈ 650 ms) and `CFG.home.cardStagger` (≈ 70 ms).
- Use a falling easing with a small settle/bounce at the end (e.g. `cubic-bezier(0.22, 1.2, 0.36, 1)` or keyframes that overshoot slightly and settle), plus opacity 0 → 1 over the first part.
- Start the fall so it lines up with the white fading out (cards can begin while the white is ~halfway gone).
- Use `Element.animate` through the `Run` (or an equivalent cancellable helper) so it is cleaned up.
- With reduced motion: no fall — a simple quick fade-in.

### Layout / responsiveness
- Must fit and look good on phones in **portrait and landscape**, tablets and desktop. Respect safe areas (`env(safe-area-inset-*)`).
- In very narrow portrait screens, keep the three cards in one row but scale them down with `clamp()`/`min()`; never let them overflow or overlap.
- Cards should feel substantial: roughly portrait-shaped (taller than wide).

### What the cards do
- **Survival**: fade the Home Screen out (cards rise/fade away), then start the existing game exactly as it played before (player placed, `Input.init(stage)`, normal camera follow). Use the normal world seed behaviour (`CFG.seed`, or keep the random one — choose `CFG.seed` and leave a comment so it's easy to change).
- **Creative mode**: for now, start the same game as Survival but pass a `mode: 'creative'` flag through to the game state (store it somewhere like `src/game/mode.ts`) so creative-only features can be added later. Leave a clear TODO.
- **Play with friends!**: disabled (see above).

### Code organisation
- New folder `src/home/` with:
  - `home.ts` — builds the DOM for the Home Screen, plays the card entrance, handles card selection, returns a promise for the chosen mode.
  - `flyover.ts` — the auto-scrolling camera over the random world (start/stop, per-frame update called from `loop.ts`).
  - `icons.ts` — the three inline SVG icons.
- Add a `#home` container to `index.html` (and to `src/dom.ts`).
- Update `src/loop.ts` so the frame loop can run in two states: `home` (flyover camera, no player input) and `game` (current behaviour).
- Update the README file tree and descriptions.

